Priestly (and Holy Water) Spoilers follow


A Priest

1.  Knows when items are normal, blessed or cursed.  This lets the Priest
    find good armor easily.  If the Priest finds an armor shop (the most
    common kind after general stores), he frequently can find gauntlets of
    power.  The best Priest I had found gauntlets of power, speed boots, and
    a blessed +7 orcish helm.  He died stupidly, however.

2.  Starts out with 4 holy water potions.  The holy water can bless any
    item in the game (or uncurse things, but this is a waste unless
    you are in dire need).  One MASSIVE spoiler:  multiple items can be
    blessed with one holy water potion.  How?  Get three scrolls of enchant
    armor, for example, arrange them so that they are listed in your inventory
    as 

    f) 3 scrolls of enchant armor

    and #dip item f) into a holy water potion.  After doing this, you will
    have 

    f) 3 blessed scrolls of enchant armor

    Blessed "add capability" scrolls add +2 - +4 (1d3 + 1)??  instead of the
    usual +1, so with these you can reduce your AC by 6-12 points instead
    of only 3 points.  (Of course you should be careful to distribute the
    enchantment among several different pieces of armor).

    It would be interesting to have empty bottles laying around the dungeon
    to fill with water (or colored liquid) at sinks.  Of course, there should
    still be the chance that you'll summon the water elemental.  Maybe
    "blessed" sinks could let you wish for a particular potion.

3.  The Priest is a martial-arts expert, like a Samurai (but not as strong or
    dextrous).  Kicking seems to be the best way to fight with a Priest,
    unless the Priest has an incredible weapon, until the Priest gets above
    about level 10.

4.  The Priest's best friend is a wand of create monster.  Why?  He'll get
    in real good with his god by zapping it a few times near an altar, killing
    and #offering the monsters, and with patience will get a named sword
    bestowed upon him.  Be in a doorway when doing this, however.


